 "last_activity": "2013-07-14T17:42:33Z",
 "messages": [
  {
   "id": "NvbINbk0-L8J",
   "from": "Roberto Pepino",
   "author": "07ce476fdba6b1e7",
   "date": "2013-07-11T17:03:57Z",
   "subject": "How can I plot the 95% Confidence Interval and medians of 3 non-parametric data sets with ggplot2?",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<p style=\"font-size:14px;clear:both;word-wrap:break-word;color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Arial,&#39;Liberation Sans&#39;,&#39;DejaVu Sans&#39;,sans-serif\">I have 3 groups of non-parametric data for which I generated 95% confidence intervals using:</p><blockquote style=\"margin:0px 0px 10px;padding:10px 10px 1px;border:0px;font-size:14px;vertical-align:baseline;background-color:rgb(238,238,238);quotes:none;color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Arial,&#39;Liberation Sans&#39;,&#39;DejaVu Sans&#39;,sans-serif;line-height:18px\"><p style=\"font-size:14px;background-color:transparent;clear:both;word-wrap:break-word\">wilcox.test(x, <a href=\"http://conf.int\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://conf.int&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792372457398000&amp;usg=AOvVaw217iDaANAl0I0arBF_ANUR\">conf.int</a>=TRUE) </p></blockquote><div> </div><blockquote style=\"margin:0px 0px 10px;padding:10px 10px 1px;border:0px;font-size:14px;vertical-align:baseline;background-color:rgb(238,238,238);quotes:none;color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Arial,&#39;Liberation Sans&#39;,&#39;DejaVu Sans&#39;,sans-serif;line-height:18px\"><p style=\"font-size:14px;background-color:transparent;clear:both;word-wrap:break-word\">Each test returned a confidence interval and (pseudo) median like this:</p></blockquote><p style=\"font-size:14px;clear:both;word-wrap:break-word;color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Arial,&#39;Liberation Sans&#39;,&#39;DejaVu Sans&#39;,sans-serif\">Wilcoxon signed rank test with continuity correction</p><p style=\"font-size:14px;clear:both;word-wrap:break-word;color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Arial,&#39;Liberation Sans&#39;,&#39;DejaVu Sans&#39;,sans-serif\">data: FAZdfrm[106:155, 5] V = 1275, p-value = 7.79e-10 alternative hypothesis: true location is not equal to 0 </p><p style=\"font-size:14px;clear:both;word-wrap:break-word;color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Arial,&#39;Liberation Sans&#39;,&#39;DejaVu Sans&#39;,sans-serif\">95 percent confidence interval: 3.468187 6.364955 </p><p style=\"font-size:14px;clear:both;word-wrap:break-word;color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Arial,&#39;Liberation Sans&#39;,&#39;DejaVu Sans&#39;,sans-serif\">sample estimates: (pseudo)median 4.789708</p><p style=\"font-size:14px;clear:both;word-wrap:break-word;color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Arial,&#39;Liberation Sans&#39;,&#39;DejaVu Sans&#39;,sans-serif\">I can&#39;t find any advice on displaying medians with 95% confidence intervals in graphical form.</p><p style=\"font-size:14px;clear:both;word-wrap:break-word;color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Arial,&#39;Liberation Sans&#39;,&#39;DejaVu Sans&#39;,sans-serif\">Ideally I would like to produce a graph like this: <a href=\"http://blogs.sas.com/content/iml/files/2011/10/barci2.png\" rel=\"nofollow\" style=\"background-color:transparent;color:rgb(74,107,130)\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://blogs.sas.com/content/iml/files/2011/10/barci2.png&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792372457398000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3Uvk66SG7bgMhL0DOlttTT\">http://blogs.sas.com/content/iml/files/2011/10/barci2.png</a></p><p style=\"font-size:14px;clear:both;word-wrap:break-word;color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Arial,&#39;Liberation Sans&#39;,&#39;DejaVu Sans&#39;,sans-serif\">Any help much appreciated</p>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "Qz0ZZYoFtnEJ",
   "from": "Brandon Hurr",
   "author": "27405c4b711a1080",
   "date": "2013-07-12T10:53:32Z",
   "subject": "Re: How can I plot the 95% Confidence Interval and medians of 3 non-parametric data sets with ggplot2?",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Make a dataframe with your Wilcox results. <div><br></div><div>Then use geom_point for the means, and geom_errorbarh() for your error bars. </div><div>Something like: </div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\" size=\"1\">ggplot(data=df, aes(x=meancolumn, y=origin, xmax=xmax, xmin=xmin)) +</font></div>\r\n\r\n<div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\" size=\"1\">geom_point() +</font></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\" size=\"1\">geom_errorbarh()</font></div><div><div><br></div></div><div>HTH, <br></div><div><br></div><div>\r\n\r\nB</div></div><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><br><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div class=\"gmail_extra\"><div class=\"gmail_quote\">On Thu, Jul 11, 2013 at 6:03 PM, Roberto Pepino <span dir=\"ltr\">&lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">roberto...@gmail.com</a>&gt;</span> wrote:<br>\r\n\r\n</div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div class=\"gmail_extra\"><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><p style=\"clear:both;font-size:14px;font-family:Arial,&#39;Liberation Sans&#39;,&#39;DejaVu Sans&#39;,sans-serif;word-wrap:break-word\">\r\n\r\nI have 3 groups of non-parametric data for which I generated 95% confidence intervals using:</p><blockquote style=\"vertical-align:baseline;line-height:18px;quotes:none;font-size:14px;background-color:rgb(238,238,238);font-family:Arial,&#39;Liberation Sans&#39;,&#39;DejaVu Sans&#39;,sans-serif;margin:0px 0px 10px;border:0px;padding:10px 10px 1px\">\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size:14px;background-color:transparent;clear:both;word-wrap:break-word\">wilcox.test(x, <a href=\"http://conf.int\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://conf.int&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792372457400000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1UadBMQB48IkGVvROCQv0X\">conf.int</a>=TRUE) </p></blockquote><div> </div><blockquote style=\"vertical-align:baseline;line-height:18px;quotes:none;font-size:14px;background-color:rgb(238,238,238);font-family:Arial,&#39;Liberation Sans&#39;,&#39;DejaVu Sans&#39;,sans-serif;margin:0px 0px 10px;border:0px;padding:10px 10px 1px\">\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size:14px;background-color:transparent;clear:both;word-wrap:break-word\">Each test returned a confidence interval and (pseudo) median like this:</p></blockquote><p style=\"clear:both;font-size:14px;font-family:Arial,&#39;Liberation Sans&#39;,&#39;DejaVu Sans&#39;,sans-serif;word-wrap:break-word\">\r\n\r\nWilcoxon signed rank test with continuity correction</p><p style=\"clear:both;font-size:14px;font-family:Arial,&#39;Liberation Sans&#39;,&#39;DejaVu Sans&#39;,sans-serif;word-wrap:break-word\">data: FAZdfrm[106:155, 5] V = 1275, p-value = 7.79e-10 alternative hypothesis: true location is not equal to 0 </p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"clear:both;font-size:14px;font-family:Arial,&#39;Liberation Sans&#39;,&#39;DejaVu Sans&#39;,sans-serif;word-wrap:break-word\">95 percent confidence interval: 3.468187 6.364955 </p><p style=\"clear:both;font-size:14px;font-family:Arial,&#39;Liberation Sans&#39;,&#39;DejaVu Sans&#39;,sans-serif;word-wrap:break-word\">\r\n\r\nsample estimates: (pseudo)median 4.789708</p><p style=\"clear:both;font-size:14px;font-family:Arial,&#39;Liberation Sans&#39;,&#39;DejaVu Sans&#39;,sans-serif;word-wrap:break-word\">I can&#39;t find any advice on displaying medians with 95% confidence intervals in graphical form.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"clear:both;font-size:14px;font-family:Arial,&#39;Liberation Sans&#39;,&#39;DejaVu Sans&#39;,sans-serif;word-wrap:break-word\">Ideally I would like to produce a graph like this: <a href=\"http://blogs.sas.com/content/iml/files/2011/10/barci2.png\" rel=\"nofollow\" style=\"background-color:transparent;color:rgb(74,107,130)\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://blogs.sas.com/content/iml/files/2011/10/barci2.png&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792372457400000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3bqU9CJDdGJ2QtQ3fZJawq\">http://blogs.sas.com/content/iml/files/2011/10/barci2.png</a></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"clear:both;font-size:14px;font-family:Arial,&#39;Liberation Sans&#39;,&#39;DejaVu Sans&#39;,sans-serif;word-wrap:break-word\">Any help much appreciated</p></blockquote></div></div>"
    ],
